---
import Docs from '@/layouts/docs.astro';
import Snippet from '@/components/product/Snippet.astro';
import {policy,request,integrationExamples} from '@/data/examples';
---
<Docs title="Your first authorization decision" description="Build AgentGuard, validate a Cedar policy, compare allow and deny, call HTTP, and verify an audit chain."><div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">QUICKSTART</span><h1>Put a policy in the path.</h1><p>Run a real Cedar decision locally, then connect the HTTP interface. The example grants one agent read access to one repository with MFA.</p></div>
<h2>1. Build from source</h2><p>Install Rust 1.89+ and the Protocol Buffers compiler (<code>protoc</code>) for the server build. For example, use <code>brew install protobuf</code> on macOS or your Linux distribution’s <code>protobuf-compiler</code> package. Node.js 20.9+ and pnpm are needed only for the TypeScript SDK and console. Build time depends on your machine.</p><Snippet title="Install the binaries" code={'git clone https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard.git\ncd agent-guard\ncargo install --path crates/agentguard-cli\ncargo install --path crates/agentguard-server'}/>
<h2>2. Initialize the store</h2><Snippet code={'mkdir my-agent\ncd my-agent\nagentguard init --name example'} title="Initialize"/><p>This writes <code>.agentguard/schema.cedarschema</code> and two policies: <code>10_admin.cedar</code> and <code>20_agents.cedar</code>. They grant broad development access. Replace both for this walkthrough.</p>
<h2>3. Narrow the grant</h2><p>Replace the contents of <code>10_admin.cedar</code> with the comment below, removing its broad permit. Replace <code>20_agents.cedar</code> with the following rule.</p><Snippet code={'// No admin grant in this tutorial.'} lang="text" title=".agentguard/policies/10_admin.cedar"/><Snippet code={policy} lang="text" title=".agentguard/policies/20_agents.cedar"/><p>The starter schema already declares Agent, Repository, repo_read, and optional session.mfa. The <code>has</code> guard handles a missing MFA field. This rule does not read entity attributes; policies that do need an appropriate entities set.</p>
<h2>4. Supply the request</h2><p>Save this as <code>request.json</code>. Application code must derive MFA from a trusted session; changing a JSON field is only a local test.</p><Snippet code={JSON.stringify(request,null,2)} lang="json" title="request.json"/>
<h2>5. Create a chain secret and authorize</h2><Snippet title="Enable a chained audit log" code={'openssl rand -base64 32 > .chain-secret\nchmod 600 .chain-secret\nexport AGENTGUARD_CHAIN_SECRET="$PWD/.chain-secret"\nagentguard validate\nagentguard --output json authorize request.json'}/><p>The request allows. Change <code>session.mfa</code> to <code>false</code> and run authorize again: it denies with exit code 2. Restore it to true before continuing. Check both process status and the decision before running any real tool; the CLI prints the decision before the audit append completes.</p>
<h2>6. Run the HTTP server</h2><p>In this terminal, start the separate server binary. It inherits the chain-secret environment variable.</p><Snippet code={'agentguard-server --listen tcp://127.0.0.1:8443 --store .agentguard'} title="Local server"/><p>In another terminal, submit the AuthZEN request. It uses subject/type/id instead of the CLI principal/type/uid shape.</p><Snippet code={integrationExamples[1].code} lang="bash" title="Call the local PDP"/><p>Expect <code>decision: true</code>. Repeat with MFA false to get false. A successful HTTP response with an explicit true decision is required to execute.</p>
<h2>7. Verify the evidence</h2><Snippet code={'agentguard audit verify --secret-file .chain-secret\nagentguard audit export --format ecs --out decisions.ecs.jsonl\nagentguard doctor'} title="Verify and inspect"/><p>Run these in the my-agent directory. Keep the chain secret and original log protected. Restart the server after editing policies; its current watcher invalidates cache entries but does not rebuild the authorizer.</p><div class="doc-next"><span>Next</span><a href="../api/">Integrate your application →</a></div></Docs>
